@<Humboldt Penguin>
@Native to Chile and Peru.
@Not to be confused with the Humble Penguin.
@They're notorious braggarts.[13][02]

@<Eastern Gorilla>
@Because a gorilla's nose print is as unique as a person's fingerprints,
@if they commit a crime you can see the evidence all over their face.[13][02]

@<Lesser Flamingo>
@Their pink coloration is gained from their diets.
@Research to find other colors of food for them is ongoing.[13][02]

@Ohoho!
@You youngsters could learn a thing or two from my grandkids.
@Remember to cherish every new memory and experience.[13][02]

@My son faked being sick to get out of school.
@So I faked being sick to get out of work!
@Seeing how happy he is makes it all worth it.
@Don't you think I'm a great father?[13][02]

@I've heard there are monkeys who can sing!
@But I've also heard that monkeys can lie.
@Would a monkey lie about being able to sing, do you think?[13][02]

@If you need a place to rest your head...
@and you're not a ghost, zombie, or monster...
@Come visit us at the cute house to the south![13][02]

@I once saw smoke rising from one of the islands off the coast.
@I wonder if anyone lives there.
@I wish I had looked through that telescope...[13][02]

@Zombies getting kidnapped...
@Animals roaming the city streets...
@All kinds of crazy stuff![13][02]

@You know...
@If it were up to me...
@I'd probably use a Duncan Factory rocket to blow up the rocks on the tracks.[13][02]

@My husband is an important man at Twinkle Elementary.
@I never pack him a lunch from home.
@He's so important, he never has time to eat![13][02]

@Have you played Super Mario Bros. 7?
@I'm still stuck on the third one.
@It's really tough![13][02]

@I love this town.
@I wouldn't be caught dead in Spookane!
@Ha ha![13][02]

@This is a restaurant, tra-la-la...
@A happy restaurant, ha-ha-ha...
@Are you feeling happy?[13][02]

@Must have lost her.
@Couldn't help it...
@Guess I'll just go and catch some speeders then...[13][02]

@They're so big!
@The way they can bite straight through bamboo is kinda scary, huh?
@What? You don't think pandas are scary?
@Couldn't you just imagine one coming out of your bedroom closet? *shiver*[13][02]

@Have you heard the one about the boxer and the tub of glue?
@There's no punchline because he got stuck on it!
@Hurhurhur! Do you get it?[13][02]

@So the guy behind the counter said their teddy bears can protect you in battle?
@What does that even mean?
@I just wanna pick out gifts for my niece and nephew![13][02]

@They say happiness is being satisfied with what you have.
@That's why I've decided to collect as much stuff as I possibly can.
@So far, it's going pretty well.[13][02]

@I wanted to re-open my business, but...
@Some really strange guy seems to have done it first?
@He seems polite, but I don't know how to ask him to leave!
@What should I do? Crud...[13][02]

@Oh, you don't need to worry.
@What kind of pet owner do you take me for?
@I made sure there were plenty of air holes.[13][02]

@<LIVE HOUSE>
@Live entertainment daily!
@Open mike every night!
@Tickets available at the Ellay Department Store.[13][02]

@I just nabbed some Live House tickets from the tool shop.
@My girl and I are gonna have a fun night out.
@But... why do they sell tickets in a tool shop?[13][02]

@A ghost appeared at my house, too.
@But, he didn't stay long.
@He thought my room was too small.[13][02]

@To the mailman searching for the address of the Rosemarys' new lease.
@If you see him, tell him they're much further to the east.
@La-la-la![13][02]

@Mom left for Youngtown.
@We haven't heard from her for days now.
@Dad and I are going there to look for her.[13][02]

@I am a clairvoyant still in training.
@However this much I can see.
@You shall return again to Union Station.
@Although I'm not completely sure.[13][02]
